    "created_at": "2026-07-14T09:46:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-07-14T09:46:42Z",
    "body": "@hsivonen provided relevant insight about the current behavior https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/8558#issuecomment-1331189029:\n\n> The reason why the CDATA stuff exists in the first place is to support copying and pasting SVG source from an XML-based .svg file inline into HTML. Since SVG title, etc., can contain a text node in SVG and text nodes in SVG can be serialized as CDATA sections, it makes sense to support CDATA sections in that context.\n> \n> OTOH, for nested HTML, we prioritize HTMLness over an SVG ancestor.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
